# task-20260814-095433-make-both-live-checkouts-auto-sync-after cadence fix
# (UMR-20260814-095405-2b53): raised from every-2h (OnCalendar=*-*-*
# 0/2:06:00) to every 5 minutes -- the same clock-based-backstop cadence
# already precedented by veridian-cron-prune-memory-backups.timer
# (UMR-20260806-134738-eec3).
#
# ROOT CAUSE this closes: claude-control and /opt/veridian/scripts are the
# two checkouts every worker/cron/dispatch unit on this box actually
# EXECUTES CODE FROM (unlike the other 7 repos this same unit also pulls,
# which are read-mostly mirrors). Real evidence gathered 2026-08-14T09:50Z
# (this task's own SPEC, independently reconfirmed live at implementation
# time): claude-control sat 16 commits behind origin/master and
# /opt/veridian/scripts sat 6 commits behind origin/main AT THE SAME MOMENT
# this unit was enabled+active -- the old 2h cadence could not keep up with
# same-day merge volume, and a transient (real, correct) refuse-to-clobber
# dirty-skip then had no automatic retry for up to 2 hours instead of
# self-healing within minutes. Six separate one-shot manual "reconcile live
# deploy drift" PRs were merged into veridian-scripts on 2026-08-14 alone to
# paper over this same gap by hand, each time reopening within minutes.
#
# This is a cadence change to the ALREADY Owner-authorized unit #1
# (sync-repos) -- not a new unit under the ~/.config/systemd/user/README.md
# closed-set STANDING RULE ("a new periodic need that fits one of these ...
# goes in ... inside the matching existing unit").
[Unit]
Description=Run veridian-cron-sync-repos on its scheduled cadence (jittered -- see the paired .service for why)

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*:0/5
RandomizedDelaySec=30
AccuracySec=10s
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
